IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nsw-nouns`
IMPORT `nsw-interpretation-time`

-- Interpretation Act 1987 (New South Wales), Part 3 Commencement of Acts and instruments: sections 22 to 26.
-- The days and the moment of commencement (sections 23(1), 23(5) and 24) are computed in nsw-interpretation-time.l4,
-- which this module calls; the rest of Part 3 is here.

§ `Part 3 Commencement of Acts and instruments`

§§ `22 References to enactment etc of Acts`

-- src:211 | (1) In any Act or instrument, a reference to the enactment of an Act or the passing of an Act is a reference to the fact of the Act's having received the Royal Assent.
@ref s 22(1) (src:211)
GIVEN `the reference is to the enactment of an Act or the passing of an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act has received the Royal Assent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(1) the enactment or passing of the Act has taken place` MEANS
    IF `the reference is to the enactment of an Act or the passing of an Act`
    THEN JUST `the Act has received the Royal Assent`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:212 | (2) The date purporting to be the date of assent to an Act, as appearing on a copy of the Act published on the NSW legislation website, is admissible in any legal proceedings as evidence of the date of assent to the Act.
@ref s 22(2) (src:212)
GIVEN `the date purporting to be the date of assent appears on a copy of the Act published on the NSW legislation website` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(2) the date purporting to be the date of assent is admissible in legal proceedings as evidence of the date of assent` MEANS
    IF `the date purporting to be the date of assent appears on a copy of the Act published on the NSW legislation website` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `23 Commencement of Acts`

-- src:219 | (2) The Governor may, by proclamation, appoint a day for the commencement of an Act that does not provide for its commencement, being a day that occurs—
-- src:220 | (a) no earlier than the date of assent to the Act, and
-- src:221 | (b) no later than the day occurring 28 days after the date of assent to the Act.
@ref s 23(2) (src:219-221)
GIVEN `the Act provides for its commencement` IS A BOOLEAN
      assent IS A DATE
      appointed IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23(2) the Governor may by proclamation appoint the day for the commencement of the Act` MEANS
    IF `the Act provides for its commencement`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`s 23(2) the day appointed is no earlier than the date of assent and no later than the day occurring 28 days after` assent appointed)

-- src:222 | (3) A power to appoint by proclamation a day on which an Act shall commence does not include power to appoint a day prior to the day on which the proclamation appointing the day is published.
@ref s 23(3) (src:222)
GIVEN appointed IS A DATE
      `the day on which the proclamation appointing the day is published` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23(3) the power to appoint a day extends to a day prior to the day on which the proclamation appointing it is published` MEANS
    IF Day appointed LESS THAN Day `the day on which the proclamation appointing the day is published`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:223 | (4) A power to appoint by proclamation a day on which an Act shall commence does not include power to appoint different days for different portions of the Act unless express provision is made in the Act for that purpose.
@ref s 23(4) (src:223)
GIVEN `express provision is made in the Act for the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23(4) the power to appoint a day includes power to appoint different days for different portions of the Act` MEANS
    `express provision is made in the Act for the purpose`

-- src:224 | (4A) A power to appoint by proclamation different days for the commencement of different portions of an Act includes the power to appoint different days for the commencement of the repeal of different portions of any previous Act or instrument repealed by a provision of the Act.
@ref s 23(4A) (src:224)
GIVEN `the power is to appoint different days for the commencement of different portions of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the days are for the commencement of the repeal of different portions of a previous Act or instrument repealed by a provision of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23(4A) the power includes power to appoint different days for the repeal of different portions of the previous Act or instrument` MEANS
    IF `the power is to appoint different days for the commencement of different portions of the Act` AND `the days are for the commencement of the repeal of different portions of a previous Act or instrument repealed by a provision of the Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:225 | (5) A proclamation appointing a day on which an Act shall commence does not fail merely because the proclamation is not published until after that day but, in that event, the Act shall not commence on that day but shall commence—
@ref s 23(5) chapeau (src:225)
GIVEN appointed IS A DATE
      published IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23(5) the proclamation appointing the day fails merely because it is published after that day` MEANS
    IF Day published GREATER THAN Day appointed THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:231 | (6) An Act may be referred to by its short title (or name) even though the provision that specifies the short title (or name) has not commenced.
@ref s 23(6) (src:231)
GIVEN `the provision that specifies the short title (or name) has commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23(6) the Act may be referred to by its short title or name` MEANS
    IF `the provision that specifies the short title (or name) has commenced` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:232 | (7) If an Act provides for its commencement, whether by proclamation under the Act or otherwise—
-- src:233 | (a) that provision has effect for the purposes of subsection (1) (b), and
-- src:234 | (b) in the case of an Act that provides for its commencement by proclamation under the Act—such a proclamation may be made and shall have effect,
-- src:235 | even though that provision has not commenced.
@ref s 23(7) (src:232-235)
GIVEN `the Act provides for its commencement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23(7) that provision has effect for section 23(1)(b) even though it has not commenced` MEANS
    IF `the Act provides for its commencement` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:236 | (8) In this section, published means published on the NSW legislation website.
@ref s 23(8) (src:236)
GIVEN `it is published on the NSW legislation website` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23(8) in section 23 the thing is published` MEANS
    `it is published on the NSW legislation website`

§§ `25 References to commencement of Acts and instruments`

-- src:241 | 25 References to commencement of Acts and instruments
-- src:242 | If an Act or instrument provides that all of its provisions, with specified exceptions, shall commence, or be deemed to have commenced, at the same time, a reference in any other Act or instrument to the commencement of the firstmentioned Act or instrument shall be read as a reference to the commencement of all of its provisions, with those specified exceptions.
@ref s 25 (src:241-242)
GIVEN `the Act or instrument provides that all of its provisions, with specified exceptions, commence at the same time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reference is in another Act or instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25 the reference to the commencement is read as a reference to the commencement of all of its provisions, with those exceptions` MEANS
    IF `the Act or instrument provides that all of its provisions, with specified exceptions, commence at the same time` AND `the reference is in another Act or instrument`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `26 Exercise of certain powers between enactment and commencement of Acts and making and commencement of instruments`

-- src:245 | (1) If an Act (in this section referred to as the Act concerned) that does not commence on its enactment would, had it commenced—
-- src:246 | (a) confer a power, or
-- src:247 | (b) amend some other Act in such a manner that the other Act, as amended, would confer a power,
-- src:248 | that must or may be exercised by the making of an instrument of a legislative or administrative character, then—
-- src:249 | (c) such an instrument may be made, and
-- src:250 | (d) any thing may be done for the purpose of enabling such an instrument to be made or of bringing such an instrument into effect,
-- src:251 | before the Act concerned commences, as if the Act concerned had commenced.
@ref s 26(1) (src:245-251)
GIVEN `the Act concerned does not commence on its enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `had it commenced it would confer a power, or amend another Act so that the other Act as amended would confer a power` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power must or may be exercised by the making of an instrument of a legislative or administrative character` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26(1) the instrument may be made and things done before the Act concerned commences as if it had commenced` MEANS
    IF     `the Act concerned does not commence on its enactment`
       AND `had it commenced it would confer a power, or amend another Act so that the other Act as amended would confer a power`
       AND `the power must or may be exercised by the making of an instrument of a legislative or administrative character`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:252 | (2) A provision of an instrument made by virtue of subsection (1) shall take effect—
-- src:253 | (a) on the day on which the Act concerned commences, or
-- src:254 | (b) on the day on which the provision would have taken effect had the Act concerned commenced when the instrument was made,
-- src:255 | whichever is the later.
@ref s 26(2) (src:252-255)
GIVEN `the day the Act concerned commences` IS A DATE
      `the day the provision would have taken effect had the Act concerned commenced when the instrument was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 26(2) the day the provision of the instrument takes effect` MEANS
    IF Day `the day the Act concerned commences` AT LEAST Day `the day the provision would have taken effect had the Act concerned commenced when the instrument was made`
    THEN `the day the Act concerned commences`
    ELSE `the day the provision would have taken effect had the Act concerned commenced when the instrument was made`

-- src:256 | (3) If—
-- src:257 | (a) this section applies to an Act that would, had it commenced, amend some other Act as referred to in subsection (1) (b), and
-- src:258 | (b) the other Act has not commenced,
-- src:259 | this section has effect as if the references in subsections (1) and (2) to the commencement of the Act concerned were references to the commencement of the other Act, as amended by the Act concerned.
@ref s 26(3) (src:256-259)
GIVEN `the Act concerned would amend some other Act as referred to in subsection (1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other Act has not commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the commencement of the Act concerned` IS A DATE
      `the commencement of the other Act, as amended by the Act concerned` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 26(3) the commencement to which the references in subsections (1) and (2) are references` MEANS
    IF `the Act concerned would amend some other Act as referred to in subsection (1)(b)` AND `the other Act has not commenced`
    THEN `the commencement of the other Act, as amended by the Act concerned`
    ELSE `the commencement of the Act concerned`

-- src:260 | (4) This section applies to an instrument that does not commence on its making in the same way as it applies to an Act that does not commence on its enactment. For that purpose, a reference in this section to an amendment of some other Act includes a reference to an amendment of some other instrument.
@ref s 26(4) (src:260)
GIVEN `the instrument does not commence on its making` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26(4) section 26 applies to the instrument in the same way as to an Act that does not commence on its enactment` MEANS
    IF `the instrument does not commence on its making` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Tests: Part 3`

-- s 22
#ASSERT `s 22(1) the enactment or passing of the Act has taken place` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22(1) the enactment or passing of the Act has taken place` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 22(1) the enactment or passing of the Act has taken place` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 22(2) the date purporting to be the date of assent is admissible in legal proceedings as evidence of the date of assent` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22(2) the date purporting to be the date of assent is admissible in legal proceedings as evidence of the date of assent` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 23(2): assent 10 June 2026; the window runs to 8 July 2026
#ASSERT `s 23(2) the Governor may by proclamation appoint the day for the commencement of the Act` FALSE (Date 10 6 2026) (Date 8 7 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23(2) the Governor may by proclamation appoint the day for the commencement of the Act` FALSE (Date 10 6 2026) (Date 9 7 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23(2) the Governor may by proclamation appoint the day for the commencement of the Act` FALSE (Date 10 6 2026) (Date 9 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23(2) the Governor may by proclamation appoint the day for the commencement of the Act` TRUE (Date 10 6 2026) (Date 8 7 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 23(3)
#ASSERT `s 23(3) the power to appoint a day extends to a day prior to the day on which the proclamation appointing it is published` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 2 7 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23(3) the power to appoint a day extends to a day prior to the day on which the proclamation appointing it is published` (Date 2 7 2026) (Date 2 7 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 23(3) the power to appoint a day extends to a day prior to the day on which the proclamation appointing it is published` (Date 3 7 2026) (Date 2 7 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 23(4) and (4A)
#ASSERT `s 23(4) the power to appoint a day includes power to appoint different days for different portions of the Act` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23(4) the power to appoint a day includes power to appoint different days for different portions of the Act` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23(4A) the power includes power to appoint different days for the repeal of different portions of the previous Act or instrument` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23(4A) the power includes power to appoint different days for the repeal of different portions of the previous Act or instrument` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 23(4A) the power includes power to appoint different days for the repeal of different portions of the previous Act or instrument` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 23(5)
#ASSERT `s 23(5) the proclamation appointing the day fails merely because it is published after that day` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 5 7 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23(5) the proclamation appointing the day fails merely because it is published after that day` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 23(5) the proclamation appointing the day fails merely because it is published after that day` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 23(6), (7), (8)
#ASSERT `s 23(6) the Act may be referred to by its short title or name` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23(6) the Act may be referred to by its short title or name` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 23(7) that provision has effect for section 23(1)(b) even though it has not commenced` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23(7) that provision has effect for section 23(1)(b) even though it has not commenced` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23(8) in section 23 the thing is published` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23(8) in section 23 the thing is published` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- s 25
#ASSERT `s 25 the reference to the commencement is read as a reference to the commencement of all of its provisions, with those exceptions` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 25 the reference to the commencement is read as a reference to the commencement of all of its provisions, with those exceptions` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 25 the reference to the commencement is read as a reference to the commencement of all of its provisions, with those exceptions` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 26
#ASSERT `s 26(1) the instrument may be made and things done before the Act concerned commences as if it had commenced` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 26(1) the instrument may be made and things done before the Act concerned commences as if it had commenced` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 26(1) the instrument may be made and things done before the Act concerned commences as if it had commenced` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 26(1) the instrument may be made and things done before the Act concerned commences as if it had commenced` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the later of the two days
#ASSERT `s 26(2) the day the provision of the instrument takes effect` (Date 1 9 2026) (Date 15 8 2026) EQUALS Date 1 9 2026
#ASSERT `s 26(2) the day the provision of the instrument takes effect` (Date 1 9 2026) (Date 15 9 2026) EQUALS Date 15 9 2026
#ASSERT `s 26(2) the day the provision of the instrument takes effect` (Date 1 9 2026) (Date 1 9 2026) EQUALS Date 1 9 2026
#ASSERT `s 26(3) the commencement to which the references in subsections (1) and (2) are references` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 9 2026) (Date 1 10 2026) EQUALS Date 1 10 2026
#ASSERT `s 26(3) the commencement to which the references in subsections (1) and (2) are references` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 9 2026) (Date 1 10 2026) EQUALS Date 1 9 2026
#ASSERT `s 26(3) the commencement to which the references in subsections (1) and (2) are references` FALSE TRUE (Date 1 9 2026) (Date 1 10 2026) EQUALS Date 1 9 2026
#ASSERT `s 26(4) section 26 applies to the instrument in the same way as to an Act that does not commence on its enactment` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 26(4) section 26 applies to the instrument in the same way as to an Act that does not commence on its enactment` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
